s mathematically, but the timing of recognition (which the XBRL data does not disclose by vintage) remains the critical unknown.\n\nThe FCF situation is structurally unsustainable in isolation. Q1 2026 FCF of -$4.71B against a current cash balance of $3.02B means CoreWeave is burning through its liquidity rapidly. With $17.8B in total debt (D/E of 3.75) and quarterly interest expense running at $0.54B, the company is in a capital-raise dependency cycle. The IPO proceeds and ongoing credit facilities are bridging the gap, but at a beta of 7.8, any sentiment shift in AI infrastructure spending creates acute refinancing risk.\n\nAnalyst consensus sits at Buy with a $127.47 average target (22.8% upside), but the distribution is wide ($67-$160) reflecting genuine disagreement about the margin inflection point and CapEx duration. The FMP fundamental score of D+ (1/5) captures the balance sheet stress accurately. The gross margin trajectory — not the revenue trajectory — is the variable that will determine whether this is a 2028 earnings story or a dilution/distress story. If margins stabilize at 65% and revenue hits $33B by 2027 with operating leverage materializing, the thesis works. If margins continue deteriorating into the low 60s as power and depreciation escalate faster than revenue, the losses deepen materially.",
